  "_doc": "M7 G-C1: AI difficulty preset registry. 6 archetypes (rifleman/sniper/assault/engineer/medic/spotter) × 4 difficulties (cakewalk/tough_crowd/veteran/hardcore) = 24 archetype-specific entries. M17 adds the hardcore tier (0.4× TTD + permadeath) mirroring the cf-ai DifficultyPreset::builtin(\"hardcore\") arm; each archetype's hardcore row extends its own veteran curve (faster aim, tighter miss, longer memory, lower retreat floor). M14 audit pass 2 (GAP-M7-04): Spotter rows added to match the M7 6-archetype roster (previously the registry only had 5 archetypes despite cf-ai shipping Spotter as the 6th archetype). Each entry carries archetype_id + difficulty_id + display name + M2 legacy AI tuning fields (hp, aim_settle_ticks, miss_chance, sight_range, sight_fov_degrees, hearing_radius, memory_decay_ticks, reload_ms, retreat_hp_pct) + M7 friend-feedback normalized multipliers (hp_multiplier, damage_multiplier, reaction_time_ticks, fov_degrees, hearing_range) + the three M7 spec extension fields. Spotter has the widest fov (220° tough_crowd) + longest sight range (520u) but low cover_seek_radius (24u tough_crowd) since spotters lurk at vantage points. The cf-ai builtin() fallback still resolves the three legacy ids (cakewalk/tough_crowd/veteran) for engines that load the M2 baseline shape.",
